From 991e00674b02c64991db3976384aac32da5b9d2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@lmepisowifi.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 05:21:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix rate validity not stacking + coin-expired
 finalization rework

Same fix as tmwim2-2050-g40's commit of the same name, applied here
directly from that commit's diff - only the license-header repo URL
adapted, no other PGN-specific divergence found in these 3 files.

  - hotspot/ratevalidity.sh: rv_grant() previously took the EARLIER of
    an existing (still-active) deadline vs. a new top-up's deadline
    when merging two validity windows - conservative by design, but the
    wrong behavior: a customer topping up again while their current
    validity window is still active should have that window EXTENDED
    by the new purchase's validity duration, not capped to whichever
    was sooner.
  - hotspot/cgi-bin/coin_result.sh: the same stacking fix applied
    within a single purchase - VALID_MINUTES is now the SUM of every
    validity-tier unit's window in that purchase (was: the shortest
    single unit's window).
  - hotspot/cgi-bin/coin.sh: reworked poll's finalization paths (the
    coin-expired race scenario) - adds request/response debug logging
    to /tmp/coinsh.log, checks RESULT_PATH earlier/more directly across
    all three rescue branches, and folds the hard-timeout and
    active:false-with-no-.result paths into a single "complete" status
    response instead of the old dedicated "expired" one.

Note (not fixed here, flagging only): that last change leaves
hotspot/index.html's `d.status === 'expired'` branch (the one showing
"Coinslot disconnected, but your N peso(s) were saved as time.") dead
for those two rescue paths, since coin.sh no longer sends "expired" for
them - they now go through the "complete" branch instead, which also
hardcodes minutes to 0 rather than calling _calc_time() like the other
five call sites in this same file still do. A customer whose coins get
rescued via either of those two specific paths will now see "No time
granted, there wasn't enough coins inserted." even though the amount
was actually banked successfully. Left as-is here to mirror
tmwim2-2050-g40's current main exactly, per this sync's purpose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
